// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/library-from-a-cdn.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeLibraryFromACdn(path: "/recipes/library-from-a-cdn", title: "Load a library from a CDN — Recipes", description: "Load a JavaScript library from another origin with meta.scripts: in order, async or after the page, pinned by a hash, allowed by the policy.") {
    RecipeShell("Load a library from a CDN", summary: "To use a library from another origin, list its URL in `meta.scripts`. The compiler never fetches anything, so it cannot read a file on another origin; a script of your own calls the library instead. This page throws confetti with the `canvas-confetti` library when the reader presses a button:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works"), Anchor(id: "troubleshooting", label: "Troubleshooting"), Anchor(id: "variations", label: "Variations")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Draw a chart from a library", to: "/recipes/chart-from-a-library"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Call your own JavaScript", to: "/recipes/call-your-own-script"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Place a custom element from a library", to: "/recipes/place-a-custom-element")], source: "md-docs/recipes/library-from-a-cdn.md", how: true, hasVariations: true, project: { "src/celebrate.js": #"// src/celebrate.js
/** Throw confetti up from the bottom of the window. */
function celebrate() {
  if (typeof confetti === "undefined") return; // not arrived yet
  const fire = confetti.create(null, { resize: true });
  fire({ particleCount: 120, spread: 70, origin: { y: 0.9 } });
}
"#, "src/pages/LibraryFromACdn.wf": #"page Launch(path: "/launch", title: "Launch", description: "A button that celebrates.") {
    Heading("We shipped").h1
    Button("Celebrate").primary { on click { celebrate() } }
}
"#, "webfluent.app.json": #"{
  "name": "library-from-a-cdn",
  "meta": {
    "scripts": [
      "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/canvas-confetti@1.9.3/dist/confetti.browser.min.js"
    ]
  }
}
"# }) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** the script `src/celebrate.js` and the `meta.scripts` setting, both shown below.")
            CodeBlock(#"page Launch(path: "/launch", title: "Launch", description: "A button that celebrates.") {
    Heading("We shipped").h1
    Button("Celebrate").primary { on click { celebrate() } }
}"#, title: "wf")
            Markdown("This script calls the library:")
            CodeBlock(#"// src/celebrate.js
/** Throw confetti up from the bottom of the window. */
function celebrate() {
  if (typeof confetti === "undefined") return; // not arrived yet
  const fire = confetti.create(null, { resize: true });
  fire({ particleCount: 120, spread: 70, origin: { y: 0.9 } });
}"#, title: "js")
            Markdown("This config, in `webfluent.app.json`, loads the library:")
            CodeBlock(#"{ "meta": {
    "scripts": ["https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/canvas-confetti@1.9.3/dist/confetti.browser.min.js"]
} }"#, title: "json")
        }
        variations {
            Markdown("An entry may be an object instead of a URL, to say how it loads.\n\n- **Out of order.** `\{ \"src\": \"…\", \"async\": true \}` loads a script that nothing on the page waits for (analytics, a tag manager) with `<script async>`. Deferred scripts run in order, so a large one listed plainly would hold back the compiled code, and the page's first full paint, until it arrived. An `async` script runs whenever it arrives instead. A module, or a script whose `globals` your `.wf` code calls, cannot be `async` (`E111`).\n- **After the page.** `\{ \"src\": \"…\", \"load\": \"after\" \}` puts no tag in the HTML at all: the runtime requests the script once the page has loaded and drawn its first frame. A browser fetches everything a page names while it loads, and a page's speed is measured against what it asked for before it first painted. A large analytics tag named in the HTML can cost a phone's Largest Contentful Paint more than a second, even with `async`. The script's origin still joins the policy. A reader who leaves within the first second is not counted. The same limits as `async` apply (`E111`). The confetti above could load this way too, since nothing calls it until a press, and `celebrate` does nothing if pressed before it arrives.\n- **As a module.** `\{ \"src\": \"https://…/confetti.mjs\", \"module\": true, \"as\": \"Confetti\" \}` imports an ES module and puts its exports on `window.Confetti`. Most CDNs also serve a plain build, which needs neither key.\n- **Called from `.wf` directly.** `\{ \"src\": \"…\", \"globals\": [\"confetti\"] \}` puts the names a library defines in scope, each typed `Any`, because the compiler cannot see their shape. A class among them is constructed when called.")

        }
        Markdown("Press **Celebrate** and confetti bursts up from the bottom of the window.\n\nAn entry in `meta.scripts` loads this way:\n\n- **In order.** The build links each entry with `<script defer>` in the order listed, before your own scripts and the compiled code. A library is there when the code that uses it runs, so `celebrate` finds `confetti`.\n- **Allowed by the policy.** The build widens the Content-Security-Policy by exactly the origins listed, so the policy that ships beside a declared library never blocks it.\n- **Called from your script.** `src/celebrate.js` is a plain script whose names are in scope, typed by its JSDoc ([Call your own JavaScript](/recipes/call-your-own-script)). A library that draws into an element of the page, such as a chart, is handed one by `Host`: see [Draw a chart from a library](/recipes/chart-from-a-library).\n- **Pinned.** `meta.integrity` pins a file to a hash, keyed by the same URL, and the build writes it on the tag with `crossorigin=\"anonymous\"`. A library from another origin without a hash draws a `D05` warning. The build never fetches the file to work the hash out: copy it from the CDN, or compute it from the file you tested.\n\nThis command prints the hash of a downloaded copy, to add as `\"sha384-<hash>\"` under the URL in `meta.integrity`:")

        Terminal(lines: [
                Line(command: "openssl dgst -sha384 -binary confetti.browser.min.js | openssl base64 -A")
            ])

        Heading("Troubleshooting", id: "troubleshooting").h2

        Table(caption: "Troubleshooting") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("What you see").header
                    Table.Cell("What to do").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`D05` on a library from another origin") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Add its hash to `meta.integrity`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`E111` on an entry") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Drop `async` or `load: \"after\"` from a module, or from an entry with `globals`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`ReferenceError` naming the library's global") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Check the URL; an `async` or `load: \"after\"` entry may not have arrived yet when your code runs") }
                }
            }
        }

    }
}
